# Wider Elements small scenes — isolated v4 candidate

This is a separate follow-on to the frozen opening/prose package. It is **not registered or published** and is not part of that package’s24-file manifest. Its new world ID is `elements-river-scenes-v4`; both `elements-small-scenes-v3` and `elements-river-locations-v2` remain unchanged.

## What changes

The full231-action journey now uses30 focused owned panels, each a genuine neighbouring worksite/viewpoint or an explicit later service of the same real setting. The four opening views are unchanged from v3. New close settings are the adjoining mill bakehouse, garden watercourse, millpond bank, lower tidal shore, washing corner and dry store. A dusk view represents the landing’s evening work. Later visits to the same orchard, square, landing and headland explicitly establish the new morning/afternoon/service rather than pretending to travel to a new country or pruning the old panel.

Every later scene has **zero stock grants**. Earth/Water/Air/Fire still enter once at the original opening. Hotspots retain their original chapter of introduction and belong to their real scene. No recipes, output identities, goals, lifecycles, source attributions, milestones or completed-on-entry policies change. Single-chapter scene visits use the shared state-sensitive closure, so an already-made useful object substitutes for its no-longer-needed ingredient chain. Earlier panels retain all objects left behind.

There is no arbitrary ten-object truncation. On the normal authored complete route every scene now enters with4–10 things; peaks are4–16 because legitimate creations remain tangible. The larger orchard/workshop peaks16 are the old graph’s actual work, not invented padding. Density is the arrival’s useful clue, not a hidden inventory limit or a claim that every optional experiment will fit below10.

