## Artwork and time honesty

Seven new853×1844 portraits were generated through the built-in image tool, saved with original PNGs and runtime WebPs, and inspected as actual pixels. `generation-prompts.json` and `art-manifest.json` retain prompts, style references, source paths and hashes. The stream-bank opening asset still contains no bridge/cart. The new watercourse contains no completed irrigation works, millpond no instrument/sample, shoreline no net/food/boats, washing corner no basin/washstand/soap, dry store no bins/chests/food, and dusk landing no lamps/clock/bell/boat. The bakehouse shows an ordinary architectural oven and cellar doorway, not prepared food or tools. Reused artwork represents an explicitly later service of the same setting; the one nearby kitchen-hearth station uses the existing square art, whose built-in hearth actually belongs there.

