- Four reproducible alternative preparation orders across every chapter, with no hidden sequence required.
- Both portable-cider vessels and fill-before-cover, cover-before-fill and serving-bowl-to-covered-jar alternatives using their actual local supplied objects.
- Unchanged recipes/goals/lifecycles, one stock batch lineage, hotspot ownership and every referenced asset’s existence.

Final focused results and build receipts are in this folder. The opening’s separate19-test evidence remains frozen. No new heavy aggregate is started: the parent owns the single intact integrated aggregate. No browser/iOS/native-touch/human-enjoyment validation is claimed. Canonical counts are not a promise that arbitrary optional exploration can never create more objects.

## Remaining design issues

The existing crossing-map, ceramic-float and tower families retain their previously recorded forward-intuition concerns. This is a density/cadence repair, not a silent recipe redesign. The chronology and setting changes are editorial choices supported by real neighbouring work areas and later services, not proof that every scene will feel different enough in human play. The next human test should check that the retained objects provide a useful clue and that recurring same-setting service panels still feel like a continuing place.
